This closure is the one new behavior-bearing piece of adapter code, and the doc comment above promises a precise semantic: `PropertyReader.getOverrides()` is evaluated **at dispatch time** (Java ThreadLocal overrides parity), not at attach time. Nothing in `test/` pins that — `async_job_pool_test.dart` and `cross_runtime_conformance_test.dart` have no overrides case, so a future refactor that hoists the `getOverrides()` call out of the closure (silently switching to attach-time snapshotting) would pass the whole suite while breaking ThreadLocal parity for worker engines.

Suggested regression test (fits `_registerWorkerToolTests`):

```dart
test('worker engines see overrides snapshotted at dispatch time', () {
  PropertyReader.setOverrides({'MARKER': 'dispatch-time'});
  final result = f.runScript('''
function action(params) {
    return runAsync(function() {
